    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>I already sleep eight hours and I still wake up tired.</summary>
      <p>Then the hours were never the problem. Sleep isn't a timer - it's work your brain has to finish overnight, and three systems decide whether that work gets done. Out of sync, you get enough hours but zero rest: still foggy by noon, still dragging through your to-do list, and another week of it is another week of half-finished tasks. A tracker will say the night was bad and stop there. The protocol says which of the three systems is broken, in what order to fix it, and what to change tonight - and if thirty days don't make your hours sharper, the guarantee above covers it.</p>
